parameters.prompt:
Dev tests passed for ${trigger.app_name} ${trigger.artifact_version}.

Lightwell patch: ${trigger.affected_cve} remediated via aiohttp upgrade.
CI build: ${trigger.ci_build_url}
SNOW change request: ${trigger.change_request}

Approve to deploy to production. Reject to halt deployment.

Write a concise, professional ServiceNow work note for a failed dev environment deployment. The note will be added to the change request by an automated system.

Facts:
- Application: ${trigger.app_name}
- Version attempted: ${trigger.artifact_version}
- Git SHA: ${trigger.git_sha}
- CI build: ${trigger.ci_build_url}
- Change request: ${trigger.change_request}
- Dev test failure summary: ${deploy_dev_and_test.artifacts.ao_dev_test_summary}

Requirements for the note:
- 3 to 5 sentences maximum
- Plain English, no jargon beyond standard ITSM terms
- Include: what was attempted, what failed, immediate action taken (production deployment blocked), recommended next step for the dev team
- Do not use bullet points or headers in the note itself

Output ONLY valid JSON:
{
  "snow_work_note": "string",
  "recommended_next_step": "string"
}

Write a concise, professional ServiceNow work note documenting a production deployment failure and rollback. The note will be added to the change request and may be linked to an incident.

Facts:
- Application: ${trigger.app_name}
- Version that failed: ${trigger.artifact_version}
- Git SHA: ${trigger.git_sha}
- Change request: ${trigger.change_request}
- Smoke test failure summary: ${deploy_to_prod.artifacts.ao_smoke_test_summary}
- Failed health checks: ${deploy_to_prod.artifacts.ao_failed_checks}
- Snapshot being restored: ${deploy_to_prod.artifacts.ao_snapshot_id}

Requirements for the note:
- 4 to 6 sentences maximum
- Plain English suitable for incident audit trail
- Include: what was deployed, what the smoke test failure indicated, that an automated rollback to the pre-deploy snapshot is in progress, and recommended next step for the team
- Do not use bullet points or headers in the note itself

Output ONLY valid JSON:
{
  "snow_incident_note": "string",
  "recommended_next_step": "string"
}

Write a concise, professional ServiceNow close note for a successful production deployment. The note will close the change request.

Facts:
- Application: ${trigger.app_name}
- Version deployed: ${trigger.artifact_version}
- Git SHA: ${trigger.git_sha}
- CI build: ${trigger.ci_build_url}
- CVE remediated (if any): ${trigger.affected_cve}
- Change request: ${trigger.change_request}
- Smoke test result: ${deploy_to_prod.artifacts.ao_smoke_test_summary}
- Snapshot taken before deploy: ${deploy_to_prod.artifacts.ao_snapshot_id}

Requirements for the note:
- 3 to 5 sentences maximum
- Plain English suitable for audit trail
- Include: what was deployed, which environment, that smoke tests passed, CVE status if applicable, and that the change is complete
- Do not use bullet points or headers in the note itself

Output ONLY valid JSON:
{
  "snow_close_note": "string"
}
